16 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText (The Frog King)
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 4 0 R /MCID 0 >>
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /H1
>>
endobj

17 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText (In olden times when wishing still helped one, there lived a king whose  daughters were all beautiful, but the youngest was so beautiful that the  sun itself, which has seen so much, was astonished whenever it shone in  her face.)
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 4 0 R /MCID 1 >>
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

18 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText (Close by the king's castle lay a great dark forest, and under an old  lime-tree in the forest was a well, and when the day was very warm, the  king's child went out into the forest and sat down by the side of the  cool fountain, and when she was bored she took a golden ball, and threw  it up on high and caught it, and this ball was her favorite plaything.)
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 4 0 R /MCID 2 >>
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

19 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText (Now it so happened that on one occasion the princess's golden ball did  not fall into the little hand which she was holding up for it, but on  to the ground beyond, and rolled straight into the water. The king's  daughter followed it with her eyes, but it vanished, and the well was  deep, so deep that the bottom could not be seen.)
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 4 0 R /MCID 3 >>
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

20 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText (At this she began to cry, and cried louder and louder, and could not be  comforted. And as she thus lamented someone called to her:)
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 4 0 R /MCID 4 >>
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

22 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText ("What ails you, king's daughter? You weep so that even a stone would  show pity.")
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 4 0 R /MCID 5 >>
 /P 21 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

21 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /K 22 0 R
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /BlockQuote
>>
endobj

23 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText (She looked round to the side from whence the voice came, and saw a frog  stretching forth its big, ugly head from the water.)
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 4 0 R /MCID 6 >>
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

25 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText ("Ah, old water-splasher, is it you?" she said. "I am weeping for my  golden ball, which has fallen into the well.")
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 4 0 R /MCID 7 >>
 /P 24 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

24 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /K 25 0 R
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /BlockQuote
>>
endobj

27 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText ("Be quiet, and do not weep," answered the frog. "I can help you, but  what will you give me if I bring back your plaything to you?")
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 6 0 R /MCID 0 >>
 /P 26 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

26 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /K 27 0 R
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /BlockQuote
>>
endobj

29 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText ("Whatever you will have, dear frog," said she, "my clothes, my pearls  and jewels, and even the golden crown which I am wearing.")
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 6 0 R /MCID 1 >>
 /P 28 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

28 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /K 29 0 R
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /BlockQuote
>>
endobj

30 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText (The frog answered:)
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 6 0 R /MCID 2 >>
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

32 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText ("I do not care for your clothes, your pearls and jewels, nor for your  golden crown, but if you will love me and let me be your companion  and play-fellow, and sit by you at your little table, and eat off  your little golden plate, and drink out of your little cup, and sleep  in your little bed „ if you will promise me this I will go down below,  and bring you your golden ball up again.")
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 6 0 R /MCID 3 >>
 /P 31 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

31 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /K 32 0 R
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /BlockQuote
>>
endobj

33 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText ("Oh yes," said she, "I promise you all you wish, if you will but bring  me my ball back again." But she thought, "How the silly frog does talk!  All he does is to sit in the water with the other frogs, and croak. He  can be no companion to any human being!")
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 6 0 R /MCID 4 >>
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

34 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText (But the frog when he had received this promise, put his head into the  water and sank down; and in a short while came swimming up again with  the ball in his mouth, and threw it on the grass.)
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 6 0 R /MCID 5 >>
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

35 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText (The king's daughter was delighted to see her pretty plaything once more,  and picked it up, and ran away with it.)
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 6 0 R /MCID 6 >>
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

37 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText ("Wait, wait," said the frog. "Take me with you. I can't run as you  can.")
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 6 0 R /MCID 7 >>
 /P 36 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

36 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /K 37 0 R
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /BlockQuote
>>
endobj

38 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText (But what did it avail him to scream his croak, croak, after her, as  loudly as he could? She did not listen to it, but ran home and soon  forgot the poor frog, who was forced to go back into his well again.)
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 6 0 R /MCID 8 >>
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

39 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText (The Promise)
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 8 0 R /MCID 0 >>
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /H2
>>
endobj

40 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText (The next day when she had seated herself at table with the king and all  the courtiers, and was eating from her little golden plate, something  came creeping splish splash, splish splash, up the marble staircase,  and when it had got to the top, it knocked at the door and cried:)
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 8 0 R /MCID 1 >>
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

42 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText ("Princess, youngest princess, open the door for me.")
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 8 0 R /MCID 2 >>
 /P 41 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

41 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /K 42 0 R
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /BlockQuote
>>
endobj

43 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText (She ran to see who was outside, but when she opened the door, there sat  the frog in front of it. Then she slammed the door to, in great haste,  sat down to dinner again, and was quite frightened.)
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 8 0 R /MCID 3 >>
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

44 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText (The king saw plainly that her heart was beating violently, and said:)
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 8 0 R /MCID 4 >>
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

46 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText ("My child, what are you so afraid of? Is there perhaps a giant outside  who wants to carry you away?")
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 8 0 R /MCID 5 >>
 /P 45 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

45 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /K 46 0 R
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /BlockQuote
>>
endobj

48 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText ("Ah, no," replied she. "It is no giant but a disgusting frog.")
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 8 0 R /MCID 6 >>
 /P 47 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

47 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /K 48 0 R
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /BlockQuote
>>
endobj

50 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText ("What does a frog want with you?")
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 8 0 R /MCID 7 >>
 /P 49 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

49 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /K 50 0 R
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /BlockQuote
>>
endobj

52 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText ("Ah, dear father, yesterday as I was in the forest sitting by the well,  playing, my golden ball fell into the water. And because I cried so,  the frog brought it out again for me, and because he so insisted, I  promised him he should be my companion, but I never thought he would  be able to come out of his water! And now he is outside there, and  wants to come in to me.")
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 8 0 R /MCID 8 >>
 /P 51 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

51 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /K 52 0 R
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /BlockQuote
>>
endobj

53 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText (In the meantime it knocked a second time, and cried:)
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 8 0 R /MCID 9 >>
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

55 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText ("Princess! Youngest princess!Open the door for me!Do you not know what you said to meyesterday by the cool waters of the well?Princess, youngest princess!Open the door for me!")
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 10 0 R /MCID 0 >>
 /P 54 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

54 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /K 55 0 R
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /BlockQuote
>>
endobj

56 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText (Then said the king:)
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 10 0 R /MCID 1 >>
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

58 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText ("That which you have promised must you perform. Go and let him in.")
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 10 0 R /MCID 2 >>
 /P 57 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

57 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /K 58 0 R
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /BlockQuote
>>
endobj

59 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText (She went and opened the door, and the frog hopped in and followed her,  step by step, to her chair. There he sat and cried:)
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 10 0 R /MCID 3 >>
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

61 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText ("Lift me up beside you.")
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 10 0 R /MCID 4 >>
 /P 60 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

60 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /K 61 0 R
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /BlockQuote
>>
endobj

62 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText (She delayed, until at last the king commanded her to do it. Once the frog  was on the chair he wanted to be on the table, and when he was on the  table he said:)
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 10 0 R /MCID 5 >>
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

64 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText ("Now, push your little golden plate nearer to me that we may eat  together.")
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 10 0 R /MCID 6 >>
 /P 63 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

63 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /K 64 0 R
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /BlockQuote
>>
endobj

65 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText (She did this, but it was easy to see that she did not do it willingly.  The frog enjoyed what he ate, but almost every mouthful she took choked  her. At length he said:)
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 10 0 R /MCID 7 >>
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

67 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText ("I have eaten and am satisfied; now I am tired, carry me into your  little room and make your little silken bed ready, and we will both  lie down and go to sleep.")
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 10 0 R /MCID 8 >>
 /P 66 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

66 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /K 67 0 R
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /BlockQuote
>>
endobj

68 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText (The king's daughter began to cry, for she was afraid of the cold frog  which she did not like to touch, and which was now to sleep in her  pretty, clean little bed. But the king grew angry and said:)
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 10 0 R /MCID 9 >>
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

70 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText ("He who helped you when you were in trouble ought not afterwards to be  despised by you.")
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 12 0 R /MCID 0 >>
 /P 69 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

69 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /K 70 0 R
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /BlockQuote
>>
endobj

71 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText (So she took hold of the frog with two fingers, carried him upstairs, and  put him in a corner. But when she was in bed he crept to her and said:)
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 12 0 R /MCID 1 >>
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

73 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText ("I am tired, I want to sleep as well as you, lift me up or I will tell  your father.")
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 12 0 R /MCID 2 >>
 /P 72 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

72 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /K 73 0 R
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /BlockQuote
>>
endobj

74 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText (At this she was terribly angry, and took him up and threw him with all  her might against the wall.)
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 12 0 R /MCID 3 >>
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

76 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText ("Now, will you be quiet, odious frog," said she.)
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 12 0 R /MCID 4 >>
 /P 75 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

75 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /K 76 0 R
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /BlockQuote
>>
endobj

77 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText (But when he fell down he was no frog but a king's son with kind and  beautiful eyes. He by her father's will was now her dear companion and  husband. Then he told her how he had been bewitched by a wicked witch,  and how no one could have delivered him from the well but herself, and  that tomorrow they would go together into his kingdom.)
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 12 0 R /MCID 5 >>
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

78 0 obj
<<
 /Type /StructElem
 /ActualText (Then they went to sleep, and next morning when the sun awoke them, a  carriage came driving up with eight white horses, which had white ostrich  feathers on their heads, and were harnessed with golden chains, and  behind stood the young king's servant, faithful Henry.)
 /K << /Type /MCR /Pg 12 0 R /MCID 6 >>
 /P 15 0 R
 /S /P
>>
endobj

